    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After one of the heaviest rainy seasons in three decades, the water system was pushed to its absolute limit. Dam operations and seasonal rains pushed the river past protective embankments, causing surging flows to flood homes, farms, and schools in Deir Ezzor and Raqqa. This flooding event resulted in families losing their homes and livelihoods. Rescue crews worked to save neighbors as boat teams pulled people from the floodwaters.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "result-1",
          "result-3"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The extreme weather event was something no ordinary person could prepare for. A critical piece of local infrastructure was destroyed when an earthen bridge collapsed. The community's youngest were lost to the water in a tragic drowning incident. In response, the head of state came to see the damage firsthand, while the upstream neighbor cut back the water flow to ease the burden on those downstream.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "how-5",
          "result-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-5",
          "result-4"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "When the floodwaters destroyed the places where people live, work, and learn, it was ordinary families who paid the highest price. Rescuers in boats pulled families to safety during the evacuation operation, showing the best of community spirit in a disaster. An official visit from the head of state felt far removed from the daily hardship of survivors, as the water management agreement with the upstream state offered only partial relief from the property damage.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
